{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__General_Awareness__Static_GK__Books__Authors__General_Awareness_-_Static_GK_-_Books__Authors_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_213_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/General Awareness/Static GK/Books & Authors/General Awareness - Static GK - Books & Authors - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 213 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/General Awareness/Static GK/Books & Authors","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following has authored the play 'Nil Darpan'?</p><p><b>Options:</b></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; '&#2344;&#2368;&#2354; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2346;&#2339;' &#2344;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><b>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</b></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Motilal Nehru</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375;&#2361;&#2352;&#2370;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Chittaranjan Das</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352;&#2306;&#2332;&#2344; &#2342;&#2366;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Dinabandhu Mitra</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2368;&#2344;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2369; &#2350;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sarojini Naidu</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2368; &#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2337;&#2370;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>1) <b>Background of 'Nil Darpan':</b></p><p>o 'Nil Darpan' is a Bengali play written in 1860 by Dinabandhu Mitra.</p><p>o It portrays the plight of Indian farmers who were forced into cultivating indigo under oppressive conditions by British planters.</p><p>2) <b>Historical Significance:</b></p><p>o The play became a crucial tool for awakening public opinion against British exploitation.</p><p>o It was later translated into English by Rev. James Long, leading to Long's imprisonment by the British government.</p><p><b>Incorrect options:</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Motilal Nehru</b>: A prominent Indian leader, but not associated with literary works like 'Nil Darpan.'</p><p>&#183; <b>Chittaranjan Das</b>: A lawyer and freedom fighter, known for his political contributions, not for writing this play.</p><p>&#183; <b>Sarojini Naidu</b>: Renowned poet and political leader, but unrelated to this work.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following is the author of the novel 'Q and A'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2313;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; 'Q &#2319;&#2306;&#2337; A' &#2325;&#2375; &#8203;&#8203;&#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Muchkund Dubey</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2369;&#2330;&#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2342; &#2342;&#2369;&#2348;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">MK Rasgotra</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2350;.&#2325;&#2375;. &#2352;&#2360;&#2327;&#2379;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">JN Dixit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2375;.&#2319;&#2344;. &#2342;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Vikas Swarup</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2360; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Q &amp; A was published in 2005 and is the first novel of Indian diplomat Vikas Swarup.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who is the author of the book 'HazaarChaurasi ki Maa'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>'&#2361;&#2332;&#2364;&#2366;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2305;' &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Krishna Sobti</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366; &#2360;&#2379;&#2348;&#2340;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sugatha Kumari</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340; &#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rita Kothari</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2336;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mahasweta devi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p><b>Mahasweta devi is the author of the book 'HazaarChaurasi ki Maa'. </b>Mahasweta Devi was an Indian writer in Bengali and an activist. Her notable literary works include Hajar Churashir Maa, Rudali, and Aranyer Adhikar.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following is the author of the epic poem 'Kamayani'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351; '&#2325;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2368;' &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2330;&#2351;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Jaishankar Prasad</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2351;&#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Gopala Sarana Sinha</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2379;&#2346;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mahadevi Varma</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2342;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mahavir Prasad Dwivedi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2357;&#2368;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2342;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><b>Jaishankar Prasad</b> was a prominent figure in modern Hindi literature as well as Hindi theatre. Prasad was his pen name. He was also known as Chhayavadi poet. Kamayani and \"Ansu\" are his famous works.</p><p>Kamayani literally means 'the daughter of Kama'. In Indian literature Kama denotes something more than a mere libido-sense. As Vincent Smith has rightly pointed out, it bears a combined meaning of Libido and Eros of the Greek mythology</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following wrote the novel 'Rangbhumi' the arena of life?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; '&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367;' (&#2342; &#2319;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2321;&#2347; &#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2347;) &#2344;&#2366;&#2350;&#2325; &#2313;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Abanindranath Tagore</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2348;&#2344;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;&#2341; &#2335;&#2376;&#2327;&#2379;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Munshi Pemchand</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2369;&#2306;&#2358;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2330;&#2306;&#2342;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rabindranath Tagore</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2357;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;&#2341; &#2335;&#2376;&#2327;&#2379;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Mahatma Gandhi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2343;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Rangbhoomi: The Arena of Life is a Hindi language novel by <b>Premchand</b>. The novel features an idealist protagonist inspired by Gandhian values.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following social reformers of 19th century India was the author of 'Stree Purush Tulana'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2360;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2332; &#2360;&#2369;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; '&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;' &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2341;&#2375;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Tarabai Shinde</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2358;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Swarnakumari Devi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2342;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Pandita Ramabai</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; &#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Usha Mehta</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p><b>Tarabai Shinde</b> was a prominent social reformer in 19th century India, and she is the author of the groundbreaking work <b>'Stree Purush Tulana'</b> (A Comparison Between Women and Men). This work was one of the earliest to criticize the oppression of women in Indian society, focusing on the inequalities between men and women.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who has written the book Sangeet Bal Prakash?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;&#2340; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Pandit Narayan Rao</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2339; &#2352;&#2366;&#2357;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Vishnu Digambar Paluskar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2339;&#2369; &#2342;&#2367;&#2327;&#2306;&#2348;&#2352; &#2346;&#2354;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Vishnu Narayan Bhatkhande</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2339;&#2369; &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2339; &#2349;&#2366;&#2340;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Bhimsen Joshi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2368;&#2350;&#2360;&#2375;&#2344; &#2332;&#2379;&#2358;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The correct answer is Vishnu Digambar Paluskar, a renowned Indian classical musician and musicologist known for his contributions to Hindustani classical music.</p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is the autobiography of Bhishma Sahni?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2349;&#2368;&#2359;&#2381;&#2350; &#2360;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325;&#2341;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Aaj ke Ateet</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2368;&#2340;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Aatma Parichaya</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2330;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Aarhdakatha</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2325;&#2341;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Pankhhin</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2367;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>&#183; <b>Bhishma Sahni</b>, the renowned Hindi writer and playwright, penned his autobiography titled <b>\"Aaj ke Ateet\"</b> (Today's Past). </p><p>&#183; The book reflects on his life experiences, including his childhood, education, and involvement in social and literary movements.</p><p><b>Further insight:</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Aatma Parichaya</b> &rarr; This is the autobiography of <b>Premchand.</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Aarhdakatha</b> &rarr; This is the autobiography of <b>Firaq Gorakhpuri</b>, a noted Urdu poet.</p><p>&#183; <b>Pankhhin</b> &rarr; This is not an autobiography but a novel by <b>Bhishma Sahni</b>.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following freedom fighters of India is the author of the book, 'The Indian Struggle'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; '&#2342; &#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2344; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2327;&#2354;' &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Mahatma Gandhi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2327;&#2366;&#2306;&#2343;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Motilal Nehru</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375;&#2361;&#2352;&#2370;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Vallabhbhai Patel</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2349;&#2349;&#2366;&#2312; &#2346;&#2335;&#2375;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Subhas Chandra Bose</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The author of the book <b>'The Indian Struggle'</b> is <b>Subhas Chandra Bose</b>.</p><p>This book, published in 1935, is an autobiographical account of India's struggle for independence from British rule. It focuses on the period from the First War of Indian Independence in 1857 to the year 1942, and offers insights into Bose's views on the Indian freedom movement.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which Indian singer wrote 'Raag Sarita'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2325; &#2344;&#2375; '&#2352;&#2366;&#2327; &#2360;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;' &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Kesarbai Kerkar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2360;&#2352;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375;&#2352;&#2325;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Balasaheb Poonchwale</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2361;&#2375;&#2348; &#2346;&#2369;&#2306;&#2331;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Kumar Gandharva</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2369;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2306;&#2343;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Chintaman Raghunath Vyas</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2367;&#2306;&#2340;&#2366;&#2350;&#2344; &#2352;&#2328;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>'Raag Sarita' was written by Chintaman Raghunath Vyas, a noted Indian classical musician and musicologist. He made significant contributions to Indian classical music through his writings and compositions.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who has written the book 'Fearless Governance', published in January 2021, describing her stint as Governor?</p><p>Options:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; 2021 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; '&#2347;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352;&#2354;&#2375;&#2360; &#2327;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360;' &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2346;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Draupadi Murmu</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2380;&#2346;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2370;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Baby Rani Maurya</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2375;&#2348;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2380;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Kiran Bedi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2367;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2375;&#2342;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Anandi ben Patel</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2310;&#2344;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2348;&#2375;&#2344; &#2346;&#2335;&#2375;&#2354;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The book 'Fearless Governance' was written by Kiran Bedi describing her experiences as:</p><p>&#183; The Lieutenant Governor of Puducherry</p><p>&#183; India's first woman IPS officer</p><p>&#183; A reform-oriented administrator</p><p>&#183; Her governance philosophy and practices</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who is the author of the book 'Poskem'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; '&#2346;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375;&#2350;' &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Wendell Rodricks</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2375;&#2306;&#2337;&#2375;&#2354; &#2352;&#2377;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Manish Malhotra</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2344;&#2368;&#2359; &#2350;&#2354;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Rohit Bal</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340; &#2348;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Sabyasachi Mukherjee</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2360;&#2366;&#2330;&#2368; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Poskem is a novel by Wendell Rodricks that delves into the lives of the Poem people of Goa.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is a book written by Avni Doshi?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2309;&#2357;&#2344;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2358;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">In Other Words</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2311;&#2344; &#2309;&#2342;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2381;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Burnt Sugar</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2344;&#2381;&#2335; &#2358;&#2369;&#2327;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Unaccustomed Earth</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2344;&#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2350;&#2381;&#2337; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Interpreter of Maladies</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2311;&#2306;&#2335;&#2352;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335;&#2352; &#2321;&#2347; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2337;&#2368;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The first sentence of a novel has a lot riding on it. In<b> Avni Doshi's</b> debut novel, \"Burnt Sugar,\" that first sentence is: \"I would be lying if I said my mother's misery has never given me pleasure.\" It is wonderfully striking, direct and confident, and devilishly funny. Such a voice, from a woman, rarely makes it onto the page. Women are often made to sound nice.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Match the books in List 1 with their authors in List 2.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">List 1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">List 2</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A) The Philosophy of the Bomb</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1) Sachindranath Sanyal</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B) Bandi Jiwan</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2) Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C) Pather Dabi</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3) Bhagwati Charan Vohra</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D) Anandmath</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4) Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay</td></tr></table></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; 1 &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; 2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; 1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; 2</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A) &#2342; &#2347;&#2367;&#2354;&#2377;&#2360;&#2347;&#2368; &#2321;&#2347; &#2342; &#2348;&#2350;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1) &#2360;&#2330;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B) &#2348;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2344;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2) &#2348;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2350; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2330;&#2335;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2346;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2351;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C) &#8203;&#8203;&#2346;&#2366;&#2341;&#2375;&#2352; &#2342;&#2348;&#2368;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3) &#2349;&#2327;&#2357;&#2340;&#2368; &#2330;&#2352;&#2339; &#2357;&#2379;&#2361;&#2352;&#2366;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D) &#2310;&#2344;&#2306;&#2342;&#2350;&#2336;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4) &#2358;&#2352;&#2340; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2330;&#2335;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2346;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2351;</td></tr></table></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">A-4, B-3, C-2, D-1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-4, B-3, C-2, D-1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Book</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Author</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A) The Philosophy of the Bomb</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3) Bhagwati Charan Vohra</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B) Bandi Jiwan</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1) Sachindranath Sanyal</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C) Pather Dabi</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4) Sarat Chandra Chattopadhyay</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D) Anandmath</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2) Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay</td></tr></table></p><p>The Philosophy of the Bomb - This was a revolutionary pamphlet written in response to Gandhis criticism of revolutionary violence.</p><p>Bandi Jiwan - This is an autobiographical account by Sachindranath Sanyal, a key revolutionary leader, written during his imprisonment.</p><p>Pather Dabi - This Bengali novel had strong political themes and was even banned by the British Government.</p><p>Anandmath - Famous for introducing the patriotic song \"Vande Mataram\", this book is set during the Sannyasi Rebellion.</p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who is the author of the book titled 'The Anarchy: The East India Company, Corporate Violence, and the Pillage of an Empire'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>'&#2342; &#2319;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;: &#2342; &#2312;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2311;&#2306;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368;, &#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2346;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2360; &#2319;&#2306;&#2337; &#2342; &#2346;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2332; &#2321;&#2347; &#2319;&#2344; &#2319;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;' &#2344;&#2366;&#2350;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">VP Menon</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2368;.&#2346;&#2368;. &#2350;&#2375;&#2344;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">William Dalrymple</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2337;&#2375;&#2354;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Shashi Tharoor</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2358;&#2367; &#2341;&#2352;&#2370;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Pankaj Mishra</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2306;&#2325;&#2332; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>William Dalrymple's new book, <b>The Anarchy</b>  -  of <b>how</b> a commercial company ended up controlling a vast empire.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following wrote the novel 'The Great Gatsby'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; '&#2342; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2327;&#2376;&#2335;&#2381;&#2360;&#2348;&#2368;' &#2313;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Chinua Achebe</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2367;&#2344;&#2369;&#2310; &#2309;&#2330;&#2375;&#2348;&#2375;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Harper Lee</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">F Scott Fitzgerald</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2347; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2377;&#2335; &#2347;&#2367;&#2335;&#2381;&#2332;&#2327;&#2375;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Alice Walker</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2320;&#2354;&#2367;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><b>The Great Gatsby, third novel by F. Scott Fitzgerald, published in 1925 by Charles Scribner's Sons.</b> Set in Jazz Age New York, the novel tells the tragic story of Jay Gatsby, a self-made millionaire, and his pursuit of Daisy Buchanan, a wealthy young woman whom he loved in his youth. Unsuccessful upon publication, the book is now considered a classic of American fiction and has often been called the Great American Novel.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which author wrote the Hindi novel 'Tamas'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2313;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; '&#2340;&#2350;&#2360;' &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Shrilal Shukla</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2358;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Bhisham Sahani</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2368;&#2359;&#2381;&#2350; &#2360;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Yashpal</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2351;&#2358;&#2346;&#2366;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Premchand</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2350;&#2330;&#2306;&#2342;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&bull; Bhisham Sahani authored the Hindi novel 'Tamas', which is based on the partition of India and the resulting communal riots.</p><p>&bull; Shrilal Shukla: Raag Darbari (1968), a satirical novel depicting rural Indian life and bureaucratic corruption; Seemayein Tootati Hain, a novel on social change; Vishrampur Ka Sant, a novel exploring spiritual hypocrisy.</p><p>&bull; Yashpal: Jhootha Sach (1958 - 60), a two-volume novel on Partition and independence; Divya, a novel on ancient Indian society; Dada Comrade, a novel about revolutionary movements.</p><p>&bull; Premchand: Godan (1936), a novel on rural poverty and exploitation; Gaban (1931), a novel on greed and redemption; Sevasadan (1918), a novel on women's social issues; Nirmala (1927), a novel on dowry and marriage.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following books is INCORRECTLY paired with its respective author?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Hind Swaraj - Mahatma Gandhi</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332; - &#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2366; &#2327;&#2366;&#2306;&#2343;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Gitanjali - Rabindranath Tagore</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2332;&#2354;&#2367; - &#2352;&#2357;&#2368;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;&#2341; &#2335;&#2376;&#2327;&#2379;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">The Discovery of India - Subhash Chandra Bose</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2379;&#2332; - &#2360;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359; &#2330;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2348;&#2379;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Why I am an Atheist - Bhagat Singh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2370;&#2305; - &#2349;&#2327;&#2340; &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2361;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The Discovery of India was authored by Jawaharlal Nehru, not Subhash Chandra Bose. The other pairings are correct.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following books is authored by Indu Sundaresan?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2311;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2369;&#2306;&#2342;&#2352;&#2375;&#2360;&#2344; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">The Feast of Roses</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342; &#2347;&#2368;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2321;&#2347; &#2352;&#2379;&#2395;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ajaya : Rise of Kali</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2332;&#2351;&#2366; : &#2352;&#2366;&#2311;&#2395; &#2321;&#2347; &#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">The Secret of the Nagas</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342; &#2360;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2321;&#2347; &#2342; &#2344;&#2366;&#2327;&#2366;&#2332;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">The one you Cannot Have</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342; &#2357;&#2344; &#2351;&#2370; &#2325;&#2376;&#2344; &#2344;&#2377;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;&#2357;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The book <b>\"The Feast of Roses\"</b> is written by Indu Sundaresan in 2008. It is the second novel in her Taj Mahal trilogy, which tells the story of Mehrunnisa, also known as Empress Nur Jahan, the wife of Mughal Emperor Jahangir.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who among the following is the author of the book 'The Coalition Years'?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; '&#2342; &#2325;&#2379;&#2319;&#2354;&#2367;&#2358;&#2344; &#2311;&#2351;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360;' (The Coalition Years) &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2326;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Giani Zail Singh</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2332;&#2364;&#2376;&#2354; &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2361;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">APJ Abdul Kalam</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;.&#2346;&#2368;.&#2332;&#2375;. &#2309;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2354;&#2366;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Pranab Mukherjee</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2348; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">KR Narayanan</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;.&#2310;&#2352;. &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2339;&#2344;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>In his book 'The Coalition Years', former president <b>Pranab Mukherjee</b>, had disfavoured the Congress' 2003 decision to forge alliances to defeat the BJP in the 2004 general elections.</p><p>The Coalition Years begins its journey in 1996 and explores the highs and lows that characterized sixteen years of one of the most tumultuous periods in the nation's political history. It is an insightful account of the larger governance phenomenon in India - coalition politics - as seen through the eyes of one of the chief architects of the post-Congress era of Indian politics.</p><p><b>Author Pranab Mukherjee</b> was the 13<sup>th</sup> President of India. A man of unparalleled experience in governance, he has the rare distinction of having served at different times as Foreign, Defence, Commerce and Finance Minister.</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}